{
    "background_story": "Sir Ezrah, a gallant knight of the realm, was known for his exceptional horsemanship and bravery in battle. However, during a fateful tournament, he was unexpectedly unhorsed by a cunning opponent. As he struggled to regain his footing, Ezrah realized that his pride had been wounded more than his body. The experience humbled him, and he began to question the true meaning of chivalry. Ezrah took this opportunity to re-examine his values and soon discovered a new passion for helping those in need. He started a charity to aid fallen knights and their families, earning him a new reputation as a champion of the people. Though he never forgot his skills as a knight, Ezrah's greatest triumphs came from being unhorsed, for it led him to a path of self-discovery and service to others.",
